# AGENTS-OS v6.5 Swarm Edition - Distributed Sync Merge Policy
#
# RULE: `merge=union` is correct ONLY for append-only logs, where every line is
# an independent fact and concatenating both sides loses nothing.
# It is WRONG for stateful/checklist files: a `- [ ]` -> `- [x]` transition is
# an UPDATE, and union keeps BOTH lines, producing a plan that claims a task is
# simultaneously open and done. Those files must conflict loudly instead.
#
# NOTE ON PATTERN SCOPE: a pattern without a slash matches the basename at ANY
# directory depth. `MEMORY.md` below therefore already covers `.agents/MEMORY.md`
# and `vault/.agents/MEMORY.md`; the explicit line is kept for readability only.

# --- Append-only logs: union merge is safe and intended ---
MEMORY.md merge=union
.agents/MEMORY.md merge=union

# --- Checklist / stateful plan files: NO union merge ---
# `task.md` (root, .agents/, vault/) is checklist-shaped. Left unspecified on
# purpose so git performs a normal 3-way merge and surfaces real conflicts.
# Do NOT re-add `task.md merge=union` — see AGENTS-OS PWF review, finding K2.
